{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Brings.color_elliptic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Brings.color_elliptic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.color_elliptic_of_powerSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.color_elliptic_of_powerSum","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/color_elliptic.lean#L84-L101","doc":"**Proposition** ([`prop:color-elliptic`], elimination step,\nproved): over an integral domain, a color root `X` distinct from\nthe spacetime ratio `z` and subject to the same power-sum\ncondition `P(X) = P(z)` satisfies the color-elliptic cubic.\n\nDerived (not assumed): the elimination identity turns the\npower-sum hypothesis into `(X − z) · cubic = 0`, and `X ≠ z`\ncancels the linear factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colorCubic_key_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colorCubic_key_identity","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/color_elliptic.lean#L70-L82","doc":"**Elimination identity (proved).**  The color-elliptic cubic is\nthe difference quotient of the power-sum quartic:\n\n`(X − z) · (X³ + (z+1)X² + (z²+z+1)X + (z³+z²+z+1)) = P(X) − P(z)`.\n\nThis is the algebraic core of the reduction of the power-sum\nconditions to the cubic at fixed `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.powerSumQuartic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.powerSumQuartic","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/color_elliptic.lean#L64-L68","doc":"The power-sum quartic `P(t) = t⁴ + t³ + t² + t` whose difference\nquotient is the color-elliptic cubic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.color_elliptic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.color_elliptic","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Brings/color_elliptic.lean#L48-L62","doc":"**Color-elliptic cubic** (named constraint).\n\nFor a projective spacetime ratio `z` and a color root `X` over a\ncommutative ring `R`, `color_elliptic z X` is the proposition that\n`X` satisfies the color-elliptic cubic\n\n`X³ + (z+1)·X² + (z²+z+1)·X + (z³+z²+z+1) = 0`.\n\nThis names the admissible-color-root condition at `z`; it is *not*\nasserted globally.  An inhabitant is produced from the power-sum\ncondition by `color_elliptic_of_powerSum` below. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:color-elliptic","label":"prop:color-elliptic","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}